Conference Call Etiquette Activity - “The Call That Went Wrong (and Right!)”

Objective:

Practice professional conference call etiquette across Face-to-Face meetings, Virtual meetings (Camera ON), and Virtual meetings (Camera OFF). Teams will submit their final output via a professional email.

One submission per team – Maintain existing protocols

Phase 1: Face-to-Face Meeting Etiquette

Create a 5–7 minute role-play showing poor meeting behaviours (interruptions, phone usage, no agenda, poor body language) and corrected professional behaviours (active listening, turn-taking, clarity, closure).

Output: Do’s & Don’ts for Face-to-Face Meetings.

Phase 2: Virtual Meeting – Camera ON

Simulate a camera-ON client call highlighting mistakes (poor lighting, distractions, multitasking) and best practices (professional appearance, framing, eye contact).

Creative Option: Short clip, comic strip, storyboard, or before–after comparison.

Output: Camera-ON Etiquette Checklist.

Phase 3: Virtual Meeting – Camera OFF

Design a voice-only call showing challenges (dead air, no name usage, background noise) and solutions (verbal signposting, confirmations, structured speaking).

Creative Option: Script or call flow diagram.

Output: Camera-OFF Survival Guide.

Final Submission (Email)

Subject: Batch name -Team [Team Number] - Conference Call Etiquette

Include: brief introduction, three etiquette sections, one creative element (meme/comic/diagram/script/table), and 5–6

lines of key learnings.

Evaluation Criteria

Practical relevance, understanding of etiquette differences, creativity, team collaboration, and professional email structure.

Expectation

Treat this activity like a real IT client environment with equal participation and professional communication.
